# AutoWork — project rules

Pocket voice recorder -> ingest by volume serial -> audio quality gate -> cloud
transcription with diarization -> relevance gate -> summary email + grounded action
items in a human review queue. Python 3.11+, three deps (openai, PyYAML, pytest),
ffmpeg required. Run tests: `python -m pytest tests -q` (272 passing; keep it that way).

## Safety invariants — never weaken these

1. NOTHING here executes action items. They land in the review queue as PENDING;
   `dispatch()` refuses anything not APPROVED by a human. Plugging in a USB stick must
   not be able to write to Jira.
2. Every extracted action and every decision carries a VERBATIM grounding quote that is
   string-matched against the source transcript. Unverified = labelled, never silently
   dropped or silently trusted.
3. The audio gate runs on RAW audio only. Enhancement inflates its metric without
   adding intelligibility (measured with Demucs: metric +4 dB, transcript still garbage).
4. Metadata (date, duration, speaker count) is DERIVED from files and the diarizer,
   never model-generated. A wrong date on a work summary is worse than none.
5. Never log or print credentials, and never commit .env, audio, transcripts or
   summaries — they contain TrueContext-confidential conversation content.

## Measured facts — do not re-litigate without new measurements

- Whisper on low-signal audio FABRICATES fluent text ("*Police*" x6, "city of
  Estrella" x14). That is why the gate exists: speech_db >= -32 AND
  (speech - rumble) >= +1 dB, calibrated in tests/test_gate.py against samples whose
  transcripts were read. Do not change thresholds without new labelled samples.
- Local LLM extraction was tried and removed: gemma3:4b 358s for 1/3 items,
  qwen2.5:7b 493s for 0/3, phi4 never finished. gpt-5.4-mini: ~7s, 3/3. Do not
  suggest reintroducing local inference on this hardware.
- 16 kHz mono 32 kbps MP3 transcribes within noise of the original (Whisper resamples
  to 16 kHz internally; the recorder's channels are bit-identical). Opus 20k degrades.
- Diarization speaker labels are PER REQUEST: chunk 1's "A" is not chunk 2's "A".
  Never union labels across uploads (it reported 4 speakers on a 2-person call);
  take the max within one chunk. A 13-label chunk on a 2-person recording
  (2026-08-27 11:30, including junk `@`) is unintelligible audio, not 13
  participants — drop it, do not print it as a headcount.
- Action identity = normalised grounding quote (+ similarity >= 0.75), NOT the title.
  Titles are reworded on every model run; quotes are stable. Same-recording
  near-identical titles are still the same to-do when quotes differ (measured:
  two Dave Casal backlog items, one quote not even about Casal). Collapse those
  for digest/UI; mark_done/reject cascades to the clone. Do not identity by title
  across recordings (Andrew vs Joe Okta permissions must stay two items).
- Glossary `correct()` runs on fresh transcribe AND on cached transcript re-sends
  (`rewrite_file`). Emails also rewrite known variants at display time; that does
  not change queue identity. A second LLM "semantic parse" for names is the expensive
  wrong lever — the summariser already gets `summary_hint()` (canonical + `about` +
  variants). Do not prime cloud transcription with the glossary prompt on low-signal
  audio (measured: hallucinations get worse).
- Prompt/threshold changes must be checked against known-outcome data before shipping.
  Ground truth so far: transcripts/ + KNOWN_ITEMS in tools/compare_backends.py.

## Environment gotchas that actually bit this project

- Windows PowerShell 5.1: redirected native stderr (*>&1) becomes ErrorRecords and
  KILLS the script under $ErrorActionPreference=Stop. Python logging writes to stderr.
  Launch Python from PS via `cmd /c "... > log 2>&1"` (see scripts/Watch-Recorder.ps1).
- Tee-Object writes UTF-16; use Add-Content -Encoding UTF8.
- $PSScriptRoot is empty in param-block defaults under -File; compute in the body.
- Shell-heredoc patching of Python files silently ate backslashes twice, turning \b
  regex word boundaries into backspace chars that match nothing. prefilter.py asserts
  against this at import; prefer direct file edits over heredoc patch scripts.
- Ollama models write INFO logs mid-request; an empty transcription result is data
  ("no speech"), not an error — one empty 15s segment must not abort a 23-min file.

## Conventions

- Config in .env (loaded by autowork/llm.py:load_dotenv), never in source.
- The LLM provider is a config string ("openai:gpt-5.4-mini"); no vendor may become
  load-bearing. Executors live behind autowork/executors/base.py.
- The summary prompt is operator-editable at config/prompts/summary.txt; the schema
  and quote-grounding stay in code so a pasted prompt cannot weaken them.
- The glossary (config/glossary.yml) is the accuracy flywheel: every observed
  mistranscription becomes a variant. Optional `about:` is topic context for the
  summariser (Okta: SSO/identity/authorization — Octo/Octa in an access discussion
  is Okta). Dave Casal variants include Cazal. Comments in files explain measured
  WHY, not what.
- USB plug-in sends one email per conversation (same Outlook event only; no LLM
  topic clustering). Weekday 07:30 sends the outstanding digest. Review UI:
  `scripts\review-ui.bat` (127.0.0.1 only). Mark done drops an item from the
  morning email; no executor runs. Approve stays on the digest until done.
- `--force-keep` is a ONE-TIME override. Its sidecar is written `forced: true` and day
 rebuilds skip it; only the run that forced it passes `include_forced`. Without that
 the 2026-08-27 personal recordings sat on disk as keep=true and the next recording
 sharing their Outlook event would have merged 60k chars of garble into a work email.
- `--dry-run` is checked BEFORE the cached-transcript branch. It used to sit after,
 so a "dry" run still rewrote glossaries, wrote sidecars and queued actions.
- The relevance gate runs PER SEGMENT on both the fresh and cached paths (`keep_relevant`).
 Classifying the joined text made one recording keepable on transcribe and droppable
 on re-run. Per-recording failures (OSError/QueueError/DayError) skip that recording only.
- Tests must never reach live Outlook: stub `match_recording`. The suite was
 Dispatching COM per run and Windows logged fatal exception 0x80010001.
- Every functional change updates tests or states why none is needed. Failure-mode
 tests quote the verbatim strings from real incidents.
